      "notes": "FN method: 400°F. CLEAN 10-in cast-iron skillet; 3/4 cup sugar + 3 tbsp water over medium-low, swirl, don't stir, until golden, 10-12 min. Off heat, pack in the pear halves (crowd them; they shrink). Back on low ~20 min until the fruit soaks up the caramel. Drape the puff pastry over, tuck the edges, cut three 2-in slits. Bake 40-45 min until browned and the pears are tender. Cool only 10-15 min, pour off and reserve excess caramel, flip onto a platter, pour the caramel back, push loose fruit into place. Serve with vanilla ice cream. (Skipping the recipe's optional cranberry caramel.) Tips: firm, slightly underripe pears; clean utensils or the caramel goes grainy. Bake it in the cast-iron skillet he's bringing. It serves 8–10, so there's tart for Friday breakfast too."
